+++ b/.nestled-updates/upgrade-notes/2026-10-23-node-22-23-4-security-pin.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+id: 2026-10-23-node-22-23-4-security-pin
+title: >-
+  Node moves to the 22.23.4 security release, pinned exactly where builds run and as a floor in engines
+priority: high
+area: infra
+type: security
+delivery: code-patch
+intent: >
+  Every place that chooses a Node version moves to 22.23.4, the Node 22 security release of
+  2026-10-20.
+
+  Exact pins (the version that builds and tests actually run on):
+  `.github/workflows/ci.yml` `node-version: 22.23.4` (both jobs), `.tool-versions`
+  `nodejs 22.23.4`, a new `.nvmrc` containing `22.23.4`, and `.dev/Dockerfile`
+  `FROM node:22.23.4-slim` instead of the floating `node:22-slim` tag.
+
+  The root package.json `engines.node` goes from `^22.14.0` to `>=22.23.4 <23`. Railway's builder
+  (Railpack) reads `engines.node` before `.nvmrc`, so the old range let a deploy build on any 22.x
+  from 22.14.0 up, including unpatched ones. The new floor means no build can pick an unpatched 22.x.
+  `engines` is a floor rather than an exact pin because `.npmrc` sets `engine-strict=true`: an exact
+  version there would make `pnpm install` fail on every machine and agent box that is not on that
+  exact patch, and again on every later Node patch.
+
+  The template's README and the debugging playbook describe the new pins. Moving to Node 24 is a
+  separate, later change; this note stays on Node 22.
+why: >
+  Node 22.23.4 (and 24.22.1) fix CVE-2026-105481 (http agent data guard), CVE-2026-105482 (dns
+  resolve null bytes), CVE-2026-106069 (TLS non-canonical IP addresses), CVE-2026-106073
+  (permission model in realpathSync), CVE-2026-106074 (crypto random caches across snapshots) and
+  CVE-2026-111497 (brotli decoder). CI ran on 22.22.1 and the engines range allowed 22.14.0, so
+  both CI and Railway builds could run a Node without these fixes.
+affectedPaths:
+  - package.json
+  - .nvmrc
+  - .tool-versions
+  - .github/workflows/ci.yml
+  - .dev/Dockerfile
+  - docs/template/README.md
+  - agents/debugging-playbook.md
+verification:
+  - git grep -nE "node-version|FROM node:|\"node\":|^nodejs " -- ':!pnpm-lock.yaml' # every hit names 22.23.4 or the >=22.23.4 <23 floor
+  - node -v # v22.23.4 locally before pnpm install, or install fails under engine-strict
+  - pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+  - pnpm typecheck:workspace
+  - pnpm exec nx build api
+  - pnpm exec nx test api-utils
+agentHints:
+  - >
+    package.json is not mirrored by template promotion: set `engines.node` to `>=22.23.4 <23` by
+    hand. Do not use an exact version there while `.npmrc` has `engine-strict=true`. The lockfile
+    does not change.
+  - >
+    Find every Node pin in the project, not only the template's files: `git grep -nE
+    "node-version|FROM node:|nodejs_?2[0-9]|\"node\":|^nodejs |NODE_VERSION"` plus `.nvmrc`,
+    `.node-version` and `.tool-versions`. Extra workflows (some use `node-version: 22`), extra
+    Dockerfiles (for example a `node:22-bookworm-slim` base) and a stale `.nvmrc` all move to
+    exactly 22.23.4, keeping their image variant (`node:22.23.4-bookworm-slim`). Nix or devbox
+    `nodejs_22` attributes cannot pin a patch; leave them and say so in the log entry.
+  - >
+    Do not change Railway itself: no `RAILPACK_NODE_VERSION` variable, no dashboard settings. The
+    owner confirms after the next deploy that the build log reports Node 22.23.4.
+  - >
+    If the agent box or machine running the upgrade is below 22.23.4, `pnpm install` fails under
+    engine-strict after this change. Install 22.23.4 first (asdf, mise, nvm or fnm all read the
+    pinned files).
